{"reference":"Nehemiah 10","book":"Nehemiah","chapter":10,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Larger Sequence","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Nehemiah 10 follows confession and a historical prayer, then records the community’s binding commitments. Those commitments address marriage, Sabbath commerce, the temple charge, offerings, firstfruits, tithes, and the support of God’s house. The long list of names at the beginning therefore introduces a public, communal act rather than a list detached from the chapter’s purpose.","verse_refs":["Nehemiah 11:1-36","Nehemiah 12:1-26","Nehemiah 8:1-18","Nehemiah 9:1-38"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_nehemiah_010_10ddddae6ac669cd7d4f4e5c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}